For a NTE Workscope, in the event CFM fails to meet the Turn Around Time specified for any Engine due solely to a delay which is not excused pursuant to "Excusable Delay", and such delay directly causes the Customer to have an aircraft on ground ("AOG") or Impending AOG situation and none of Customer's spare Engines are available because they are either receiving a shop visit or installed on an aircraft operated by Customer and not by a third party, CFM shall provide or cause to be provided the following :

{Within [hours] hours, CFM shall respond to AOG enquiries from Customer, and}

{Within [hours2] hours of being notified by Customer that the above described situation exists, CFM shall advise Customer of the location of the closest available lease engine}

{CFM shall deliver or cause to be delivered, such lease engine to Customer, [incoterms], at a CFM housekeeping facility or other mutually agreed location. CFM will endeavor to provide this engine in a neutral QEC configuration. All transportation costs will be Customer's responsibility and CFM will pay Customer the fixed sum of [amount] [currency] as compensation for a roundtrip transportation from and to Europe and beyond.}

CFM's obligation to provide such lease engine will terminate when the AOG condition is corrected by the Redelivery of an Engine to Customer, subject to Customer's obligation to return the lease engine set forth below.

{Customer shall pay the hourly restoration charges and the LLP fees per flight cycle payable under the lease agreement in respect of the lease engine until the lease engine is removed from Customer's aircraft. CFM shall waive the daily engine rental fees up to a maximum of [amount2] [currency2] per lease engine, in respect of the lease engine for the AOG condition and for up to [calendar_days] calendar days after the correction of the AOG condition. Customer will commence paying any and all daily engine rental fees on the[day_number] [format] calendar day following correction of the AOG condition.}

{In the event that CFM cannot provide such lease engine in accordance with the above terms and if a leased engine is sourced by Customer, CFM shall reimburse the daily engine rental fees up to a maximum of [amount3] [currency3] per lease engine and also pay the transportation cost of such leased engine at the fixed sum of [amount4] [currency4] for a roundtrip transportation from and to Europe and beyond}

{In the event no leased engines is provided or sourced as per article above, CFM will, as liquidated damages, issue a credit to Customer in the amount of [amount5] [currency5] per Day. Such amount shall escalate on annual basis in accordance with the escalation formula set forth in FPLS, beginning on the Day after such AOG situation occurs up to the resolution of the AOG situation by Redelivery of an Engine{, up to a maximum of [amount6] [currency6] per Engine Shop Visit.}

{Notwithstanding the provisions stated above, in addition CFM agrees to grant to Customer flexibility for shop visits during the term of the Agreement, as follows:
the daily engine rental fee cap will be improved up to [amount7] [currency7] per lease engine, for a maximum of [SV_nbr] shop visits, and}
by way of compensation, for the same number of shop visits , the daily engine rental fee cap will be then reduced to [amount8] [currency8] per lease engine.}

{[1]The Guarantee will commence following the Engine's Performance Restoration Workscope, and will terminate when the Engine either: (i) requires a subsequent shop visit or (ii) exceeds the guaranteed EFH.}

{[2]The Engine must be removed for performance deterioration resulting from normal prolonged on­wing operation, with fewer than guaranteed TOW EFH. If the Engine is removed for any other reason, or is found to have suffered performance deterioration as a result of an identifiable cause other than normal prolonged on-wing operation (e.g. debris ingestion, faulty LRU's, mishandling or other actions/inactions not consistent with good practice) then the removal will net be eligible for the TOW guarantee.}

{[3]Customer required to, in accordance with the on-wing performance monitoring trends, (i) in a timely manner troubleshoot and correct where possible the adverse Engine performance reports and (ii) perform at appropriate regular intervals engine gas path water wash per the OEM Engme Shop Manual or equivalent Airframer's Manual.}

{[4]All liquidated damages paid by CFM to Customer shall be made in the form of a credit ta be applied against the applicable final invoice amount.}

If CFM fails to meet the Engine EGT margin identified, CFM agrees to provide the following remedy as liquidated damages:

{[amount] USD per each [degree] [C_F] up to  max of [degree2] [C_F2] that the repaired Engine is below the guaranteed margin and [amount2] USD per each 1 [C_F3] from [degree3] [C_F4] up to a max of [degree4] [C_F4] that the repaired Engine is below the guaranteed margin, total remedy per Shop Visit not to exceed [amount3] USD.}

{If an Engine has been accepted for Redelivery by Customer with less than [degree5] [C_F5] degrees of EGT margin, CFM shall provide a Time on Wing ("TOW") guarantee of [EFH] EFH with the total remedy by CFM per shop visit not to exceed [value] [currency] on a pro rata basis from [flight_hour1] to [flight_hour2] flight hours.}

{In the event that the actual EGT margin at the test cell after the Eligible Workscope is lower than the EGT Margin guarantee specified above and the Engine is otherwise Serviceable, Customer will accept the Engine and CFM will compensate Customer [value2] [currency2] per degree up to ten [degree6] [C_F6] missing degree. Altematively, in case the EGT Margin missing is above  [degree7] [C_F7], instead of a credit remedy for missing degrees, CFM shall provide Customer  with a Time On Wing ("TOW") guarantee as described in Article ''Time On Wing ("TOW") Guarantee" below for the repaired Engine.}

Such remedy will constitute the sole remedy of Customer and the sole liability of CFM for the Single EGT Margin Guarantee under this Service Agreement.

Upon Delivery, CFM will notify Customer of any components or [missing_items] missing from the Engine. CFM will replace such missing items at Customer’s expense as Supplemental Services, unless:
- CFM notifies Customer in writing within [hours_days] [unit] after receiving CFM’s notice that Customer wishes to furnish such missing items;-
- Customer delivers such missing items to the CFM Designated Repair Station within [weeks] weeks.  

{In order to complete the test cell run, in the event any component or Engine Controls and Accessories item is missing from the Engine, CFM may, at Customer’s request, fit its own item if available. This loan service is applicable to components or Engine Controls and Accessories with a current supplier spare parts catalog list price value lower than [value] [currency].}

{In such a case, five [days] Days shall be added to the TAT for the relevant Engine. This slave item shall be removed from the Engine before the Engine shipment.}

{For such loan service, Customer will be charged an amount of [amount] [currency] per missing item and per test cell run. CFM may, at CFM’s sole discretion, provide such loan service to items with higher value, which will be charged at [percent] percent of the current item supplier spare parts price catalog.}

{For [engine-parts] repaired and Redelivered within [months-before-expiration] calendar months preceding expiration of its [period] [contract]}
If Customer claims a defect in workmanship within {either [months-of-operation] calendar months of operation or}
[months-following-redelivery] calendar months following Redelivery, or [EFH-numbers] EFH, whichever comes first and
{Customer provides written notice to CFM of such defect within thirty [days-of-discovery] Days of its discovery}, and
{Customer ships to CFM the part or component which gives rise to the claim to the facility directed by CFM within [days] days, or, in cases in which shipment is commercially impracticable, makes such part or component reasonably available to CFM’s personnel} and

{CFM reasonably establishes that Customer’s claim is correct, CFM will provide or cause to provide, at CFM’S option, [following]: [CFM-warranty-options].}

{If any QEC or accessory had been repaired during shop visit and found fault within [EFH] EFH after installation and subject to CFM's defective performance, CFM shall pay a penalty of [penalty] [currency] per occurence.}
